## ADGM Arbitration Regulations 2015 — recognition and enforcement of
## foreign arbitral awards
##
## Source: ADGM Arbitration Regulations 2015. Sections 56–58 implement
## the New York Convention 1958 in ADGM, in close parallel to Singapore
## IAA s 31. The grounds for refusing recognition / enforcement of a
## foreign arbitral award track Article V of the Convention:
##
##   s 56(2)(a)  incapacity / invalid arbitration agreement
##   s 56(2)(b)  improper notice / unable to present case
##   s 56(2)(c)  award beyond scope of submission to arbitration
##   s 56(2)(d)  composition of tribunal not in accordance with
##               party agreement
##   s 56(2)(e)  award not yet binding / set aside / suspended at seat
##   s 56(3)(a)  subject matter not arbitrable in ADGM
##   s 56(3)(b)  enforcement contrary to ADGM public policy
##
## The shape of refusal is identical to the Singapore IAA s 31 shape
## (see `sg_iaa_s_31.catala_en`); both modules exist because (a) the
## statutory references differ and a Stage-2 simulator routes by
## tribunal-of-filing, and (b) the public-policy gate in particular is
## tribunal-specific.
##
## Used in:
##   ADGM arbitration_recognition / arbitration_enforcement claims (10
##   coded judgments cite this instrument).

```catala
declaration enumeration ADGMArbitrationGroundId:
  -- S56_2_a_Incapacity
  -- S56_2_b_NaturalJustice
  -- S56_2_c_OutsideScope
  -- S56_2_d_TribunalComposition
  -- S56_2_e_NotBinding
  -- S56_3_a_NotArbitrable
  -- S56_3_b_PublicPolicy

declaration enumeration ADGMGroundOutcome:
  -- Dismissed
  -- AllowedInPart
  -- AllowedInFull

declaration enumeration ADGMRecognitionDisposition:
  -- RecognitionGranted
  -- RecognitionGrantedInPart
  -- RecognitionRefused

declaration structure ADGMGroundFinding:
  data ground content ADGMArbitrationGroundId
  data court_outcome content ADGMGroundOutcome

declaration structure ADGMRefusalDisposition:
  data n_grounds_pleaded content integer
  data n_grounds_dismissed content integer
  data n_grounds_partial content integer
  data n_grounds_full content integer
  data overall_disposition content ADGMRecognitionDisposition
  data award_recognised content boolean

declaration scope ADGMRecognition:
  input grounds content list of ADGMGroundFinding
  output disposition content ADGMRefusalDisposition

scope ADGMRecognition:
  definition disposition equals
    let dismissed equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = Dismissed)
    in
    let partial equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = AllowedInPart)
    in
    let full equals
      number of (list of g among grounds
                 such that g.court_outcome = AllowedInFull)
    in
    let overall equals
      if full > 0 then RecognitionRefused
      else (if partial > 0 then RecognitionGrantedInPart
            else RecognitionGranted)
    in
    ADGMRefusalDisposition {
      -- n_grounds_pleaded: number of grounds
      -- n_grounds_dismissed: dismissed
      -- n_grounds_partial: partial
      -- n_grounds_full: full
      -- overall_disposition: overall
      -- award_recognised: full = 0
    }
```

## Tests — recognition granted, partial, refused.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestADGMRecognitionGranted:
  composite scope ADGMRecognition
  output disposition content ADGMRefusalDisposition

scope TestADGMRecognitionGranted:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  definition composite.grounds equals [
    ADGMGroundFinding { -- ground: S56_3_b_PublicPolicy   -- court_outcome: Dismissed };
    ADGMGroundFinding { -- ground: S56_2_c_OutsideScope   -- court_outcome: Dismissed }
  ]
  assertion disposition.overall_disposition = RecognitionGranted
  assertion disposition.award_recognised = true

#[test] declaration scope TestADGMRecognitionRefused:
  composite scope ADGMRecognition
  output disposition content ADGMRefusalDisposition

scope TestADGMRecognitionRefused:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  ## A single fully-allowed public-policy ground is dispositive.
  definition composite.grounds equals [
    ADGMGroundFinding { -- ground: S56_3_b_PublicPolicy   -- court_outcome: AllowedInFull };
    ADGMGroundFinding { -- ground: S56_2_c_OutsideScope   -- court_outcome: Dismissed }
  ]
  assertion disposition.overall_disposition = RecognitionRefused
  assertion disposition.award_recognised = false
```
